  "articleBody": "Regular roof maintenance inspections are like health check-ups for your home – they help catch small issues before they turn into big, costly problems. While some things are best left to the pros, knowing what to generally look for can help you identify when it's time to call in an expert. The key is to be proactive, especially in Texas where weather can be tough on roofs. Discounted Roofing Co. has seen countless cases where early detection during a routine check could have prevented a major headache. This quick guide will give you a basic understanding of what you and a professional will be scanning for during a maintenance inspection.\n\n### Checklist\n- [ ] Review prior roof records — why it helps understand past issues and identify recurring problems.\n- [ ] Inspect ceilings, attics, and walls — why these areas often show the first signs of interior moisture from roof leaks.\n- [ ] Examine the roof surface for visible damage — why looking for cracked, curling, or missing shingles, and exposed underlayment can indicate wear and tear.\n- [ ] Check flashings, seams, and penetrations — why these are common entry points for water if they are loose or deteriorated.\n- [ ] Inspect gutters and drainage systems for blockages — why clogged gutters can lead to water pooling and fascia damage.\n- [ ] Look at vents and rooftop equipment — why blockages or damage around these elements can affect attic ventilation and lead to moisture issues.\n- [ ] Document any identified defects with photographs — why visual evidence helps in understanding the scope of issues and planning repairs.\n- [ ] Note any accumulated debris or granule loss — why debris can trap moisture, and excessive granule loss indicates shingle aging.\n\n### How to use this checklist\nThis checklist can help you understand the key areas professionals focus on during a preventive roof maintenance inspection. While you can visually check some items from the ground, always prioritize safety and consider calling Discounted Roofing Co. for a thorough, hands-on assessment, especially for difficult-to-reach areas or suspected damage.\n\n### What to Do Next\nDon't wait for a leak to become a crisis. Use this checklist to get a general idea of your roof's condition, then contact Discounted Roofing Co. to schedule a comprehensive preventive roof maintenance inspection. We'll provide a detailed assessment and recommendations.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-03"
}